{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"Under **Rule 2a-5**, the board may designate **the fund’s investment adviser—not a sub-adviser**—to perform fair-value determinations for some or all investments, subject to board oversight.\n\nThe valuation designee must provide:\n\n- **At least quarterly, written reports** covering board-requested information and material fair-value matters, including changes in valuation risks/conflicts, methodologies, pricing-service oversight, and other material process developments.\n- **At least annually, a written assessment** of the valuation process’s adequacy and effectiveness, including testing results and resource adequacy, with material changes in responsible personnel’s roles or functions.\n- **Prompt written notification** of matters materially affecting fair value, within the board’s prescribed period, **no later than five business days after awareness**, plus follow-up reporting as the board reasonably determines appropriate. This includes significant deficiencies or material weaknesses in the valuation process and material NAV-calculation errors.\n\n**Worth knowing:** Delegation does not eliminate board oversight."}}
